scene W: {N} looks at the number and thinks first of the debts to clear and the people at home who have done without.
scene U: {N} opens a new tab and starts comparing savings accounts before the money has even cleared.
scene B: A month's pay, free and clear. {N} has been waiting for exactly this kind of opening.
scene R: {N} reads the figure twice and lets out a whoop that turns heads across the office.
scene G: {N} thinks of {grandparent}, who never had a spare month's wage in a whole lifetime of work.
- W | pay off the debts first, then give a tenth to charity | v: security, benevolence | chance: 93
- U | study the options for a week, then invest it | v: security, achievement | chance: 85
- B | take the bonus as proof of your worth and ask for a permanent raise | v: power, achievement | chance: 65
- R | spend it on the thing you have wanted for years | v: hedonism | chance: 93
- G | spend most of it on the family, starting with whoever has it hardest | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 82
- W>U | pay for the professional qualification your field recognises | v: achievement, self-direction | door | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- U>B | research a small flat to let, and put it toward the deposit | v: power (resources), achievement | binds | chance: 78
- B>R | keep it secret from the family and spend it all on yourself | v: hedonism | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: hiding money from the family; backfire: found out | chance: 92
- R>G | on a whim, take the whole family to the mountains for a week | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 88
