scene: At four in the morning, after a long night, {child} is born, small and furious and perfect.
scene W: {N} holds {child} and feels the weight of a promise nobody had to say out loud.
scene U: {N} cannot stop watching {child}: the grip of the tiny fingers, the eyes trying to find a face.
scene B: {N} looks at {child} and thinks: this one will have every chance {N} never had.
scene R: {N} laughs and cries at once, and phones everyone at five in the morning.
scene G: {child} has the family nose. Somewhere in that small face are all the grandparents, back and back.
- W | vow to be the parent this child can always count on | v: benevolence | tags: commit:children | chance: 68
- U | read everything about the first months, and plan the nights in shifts | v: security, benevolence | tags: commit:children | chance: 75
- B | start saving for the best schools in the very first week | v: achievement | habit | tags: commit:children | chance: 85
- R | throw a huge party to welcome the baby, sleep or no sleep | v: hedonism, benevolence | tags: commit:children | chance: 63
- G | bring the baby to meet the grandparents, and give it a family name | v: tradition | identity | tags: commit:children | chance: 72
- BR | hire help, and refuse to let the baby change how you live | v: self-direction, hedonism | identity | tags: commit:children | role: men | chance: 68
- BG | start a fund in the baby's name, and get the whole family paying in | binds | v: power (resources), tradition | tags: commit:children | chance: 65
- UG | track the baby's own rhythms in a notebook, and follow them, not the books | v: benevolence, self-direction | habit | tags: commit:children | chance: 75
- WU | take the baby first-aid course, and childproof the home by its checklist | v: security | mark: learned a skill | tags: commit:children | chance: 85
- WR | take every hour of leave and give the first year everything you have | v: benevolence | tags: commit:children | role: women | chance: 75
works: The first months are hard and sweet, and {N} grows into a parent without noticing.
works: {child} thrives, and the house fills with a new kind of noise.
fails: The sleepless months grind on, and {N} barely recognises the face in the mirror.
fails: Money and nerves run thin, and the first year is harder than anyone warned.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: burnout (triads from D5a)

== burnout
tier: life event
at: employer
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 22-65
per_year: 0 0 .008 .012 .01 0
drivers: stress+1 money-.3 trouble+.15
gap: 3-8
times: estimate (Part D has no burnout entry; its nearest, D68 a major depressive episode, is broader and runs about 8 in 100 adults a year): surveys find about one worker in ten reporting severe exhaustion, and perhaps two or three in a hundred a year stopping work for weeks because of it; most often in the busy middle years. Point 12 (Emren 2026-10-05): the yearly figures above are lowered to 0, 0, .008, .012, .01, 0 (child to elder): about 1 working life in 3 meets a burnout that stops work (estimate; the old rate gave 7 in 10).
likelier: long hours, a job with high demands and little say over the work, small children and an ailing parent at once, money worries
rarer: a job with control over the work, a partner who shares the load, time off that is really off
tone: trouble
life: work, body
horizon: months
roles: boss, partner, colleague, a doctor
domain: career1
rite: mature
earth: months of overwork, and one morning your body will not get out of bed
scene: One Monday morning {N} sits on the edge of the bed, fully dressed, and cannot make their legs stand up.
scene W: {N} has never let anyone down, and the list of people depending on {N} runs through the night like a drumbeat.
scene U: {N} has been tracking it for months without admitting it: the broken sleep, the forgetting, the racing heart at every new email.
scene B: {N} built this career one sacrifice at a time, and now the body is sending the bill.
scene R: {N} wants to scream, quit, run, anything but open the laptop one more time.
scene G: Even a field must lie fallow, {grandparent} used to say. {Ns} body seems to have decided the same.
- W | see the doctor, take the sick leave, and follow the plan to the letter | v: conformity, security | chance: 68
- U | work out what is draining your strength, and redesign your days around it | v: self-direction | habit | chance: 65
- B | push through on coffee and willpower; you cannot afford to fall behind | v: achievement | habit | act: push through on coffee and willpower, since they cannot afford to fall behind | chance: 20
- R | quit on the spot and walk out into the sunshine | identity | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 71
- G | take time off, walk in the woods each day, and let your body heal slowly | v: security, universalism (nature) | chance: 68
- WUR | set hard limits on your hours, and fill the evenings with something you love | v: self-direction, hedonism | habit | chance: 68
- WRG | stop hiding it, tell your family and friends, and lean on them | v: benevolence, security | chance: 75
- WBG | hand off what you can, keep only what matters, and outlast the bad stretch | v: security | binds | chance: 70
- UBR | walk out in style and take your best clients along | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: law: breaking the terms of the contract; backfire: sued by the old firm | chance: 65
- UBG | quietly pass your workload to others, and rest while they carry it | v: hedonism, security | closed: approval: colleagues left to carry it; backfire: found out, and resented | chance: 70
works: Slowly {N} sleeps again, and work takes up less room in the head.
works: Months later {N} looks back on it as the moment life was rearranged.
fails: {N} goes back too soon, and the second crash is worse than the first.
fails: The exhaustion lingers for a year, and something in {N} stays dimmer.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a serious accident or illness (triads from D5b)

== a serious accident or illness
tier: life event
at: hospital
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 .015 .012 .01 .008
drivers: harsh+.4 money-.3 stress+.2 unrest+.2 health-.2 trouble+.1
gap: 3-8
times: about 1.5 in 100 young adults, 1.2 in 100 adults, 1 in 100 in midlife and 0.8 in 100 elders a year are seriously hurt in a road or work accident (D72, data and estimate); a grave illness comes through a frightening diagnosis
likelier: youth, drinking, a dangerous job, rural roads and long drives, a harsh place to live, weak safety rules, poverty, poor health
rarer: safety laws and safer cars, a safe job, caution, money for a safer life
tone: trouble
life: body
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, friend, boss, a doctor
rite: mature
earth: a car crash or a sudden illness puts you in hospital for weeks
scene: {N} wakes in a hospital bed with a cast on one leg, a drip in one arm, and three weeks gone in a blur.
scene W: {N} lies in the ward thinking of the bills, the job, and the people at home who need {N} back on their feet.
scene U: {N} asks the doctors for every scan and every number, trying to understand exactly what has happened.
scene B: The accident was not {Ns} fault, and {N} wants to know who is going to pay for it.
scene R: {N} hates the bed, the beeping, the ceiling tiles. Every bone wants to get up and go.
scene G: Outside the ward window a tree is coming into leaf. {N} watches it day by day, healing at the same slow speed.
- W | follow every instruction from the doctors and the physiotherapist | v: conformity, security | chance: 68
- U | read every study on your condition and question every treatment | v: self-direction, security | mark: learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | hire a lawyer and sue for every penny you can get | v: power (resources) | mark: made an enemy | chance: 62
- R | laugh it off, and turn the ward into a party for every visitor | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 68
- G | rest, and trust your body to heal in its own time | v: security | chance: 60
- WUG | join a recovery group, keep a careful log, and walk a little further each day | v: security, achievement | habit | chance: 75
- WUB | plan your recovery like a project, with targets, aids and deadlines | v: achievement | chance: 72
- WBR | work from the hospital bed and refuse to lose your place | identity | v: achievement, power | closed: approval: against the doctors' orders; backfire: a relapse | tech: remote work | chance: 48
- URG | set one fierce goal, a hill to climb by next year, and train for it | v: achievement, stimulation | door | body: heavy | chance: 65
- BRG | ignore the doctors, trust your body and fight your own way back | v: self-direction | mark: defied an authority | body: heavy | closed: approval: against medical advice; backfire: a setback, and back to hospital | chance: 45
works: Month by month the body comes back, and {N} walks out of the last appointment unaided.
works: The recovery is slow but sure, and {N} comes out of it with a new respect for being well.
fails: The healing stalls, and a second operation is needed.
fails: {N} recovers, but not fully, and life has to be rearranged around what is lost.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: buying a home (cross cycle s4)

== buying a home
tier: life event
at: bank
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
per_year: 0 0 .02 .04 .03 .015
drivers: money+.6 prosper+.4 family+.3 unrest-.4 fortune+.1
times: about 2 in 100 young adults, 4 in 100 adults, 3 in 100 in midlife and 1.5 in 100 elders buy a home each year (D17, data and estimate); the typical first-time buyer in the US was 40 in 2025
likelier: a steady income, a partner or marriage, children, a growing economy, low interest rates, family help with the deposit
rarer: low money, high prices and rents, insecure work or a lost job, debt, unsettled times
tone: mixed
life: home, money
horizon: years
roles: partner, parent, the bank, a neighbour
rite: adult
earth: you sign for a house and a thirty-year mortgage
scene: The offer is accepted. {N} holds a set of keys and a mortgage that will outlast {Ns} working life.
scene W: {N} reads the mortgage contract slowly, because a debt of thirty years is a promise, and {N} keeps promises.
scene U: {N} has compared forty houses, three banks and every interest rate in the country, and still wakes at night doing sums.
scene B: Property only goes up, {N} reasons, and this one is a bargain because the seller is desperate.
scene R: {N} fell in love with the house in the first five minutes, and the bank had better keep up.
scene G: The garden has an old apple tree, and {N} can already imagine children climbing it, and grandchildren after them.
- W | take a safe fixed-rate mortgage, and never miss a payment | v: security, conformity | chance: 70
- U | study the market for a year and buy only when the numbers are right | binds | v: security, achievement | chance: 72
- B | buy from a desperate seller, well below the asking price | binds | v: power (resources) | chance: 72
- R | buy the house you fell for, even if it stretches you thin | v: hedonism, stimulation | binds | chance: 68
- G | buy in the town where your family has always lived | v: tradition, security | mark: stayed home | binds | chance: 72
- W>G | buy close to your family, so you can all look after one another | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 68
- U>W | choose the safest, best-run street in town, after months of research | v: security | chance: 78
- B>U | buy a wreck cheap, and learn to rebuild it with your own hands | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 65
- R>B | bid far over the asking price on impulse, sure the house will pay off | binds | v: power (resources) | chance: 60
- G>R | buy a cheap cottage far out in the country, away from everything | v: self-direction, universalism (nature) | door | mark: moved away | chance: 65
works: The keys turn, the boxes are unpacked, and the place starts to feel like {Ns}.
works: The first year in the house goes well, and the mortgage feels like an anchor rather than a weight.
fails: The survey missed something, and the first winter brings a repair bill that hurts.
fails: Interest rates rise, and every month the payment is a little harder to find.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a chance to start a business of your own (cross cycle s2)

== a chance to start a business of your own
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-75
per_year: 0 0 .021 .035 .028 .011
drivers: money+.4 prosper+.4 ties+.3 health+.2 era+.2 unrest-.3 fortune+.1
gap: 4-10
times: about 3 in 100 young adults, 5 in 100 adults, 4 in 100 in midlife and 1.5 in 100 elders a year start a business of their own (D16, data and estimate, Kauffman 2025); about half of new businesses close within five years. Point 12 (Emren 2026-10-05): the yearly figures above are lowered to 0, 0, .021, .035, .028, .011 (child to elder): a serious chance every few years at most (estimate).
likelier: savings, a skill people pay for, friends and contacts, a growing economy, the internet, a family trade, a partner with a steady income, losing a job
rarer: low money and debt, dependants and no savings, a recession, unrest, poor health, heavy regulation, caring duties
tone: mixed
life: work, money
horizon: years
roles: mentor, partner, friend, the bank
domain: career1
earth: a retiring owner offers to sell you the small business they built, on easy terms
scene: {mentor} is retiring, and offers to sell {N} the small business {mentor} spent thirty years building, on easy terms.
scene W: {mentor} is trusting {N} with the business, the staff and the loyal old customers, and that trust is a weight as well as a gift.
scene U: {N} spends a weekend with the account books spread over the kitchen table, looking for what the numbers really say.
scene B: To be one's own boss and keep every penny of the profit: {N} has wanted this since the first day of the first job.
scene R: {Ns} heart is pounding. This is the leap {N} has talked about for fifteen years.
scene G: The shop has stood on the same corner for thirty years, and the old customers come in as much to talk as to buy.
- W | take it on, and keep every promise made to the staff and the old customers | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: kept your word | tags: commit:career | chance: 55
- U | take it on only after three months on the books and a full business plan | binds | v: security, achievement | tags: commit:career | chance: 72
- B | take it, cut the dead weight, and run it hard for profit | identity | v: power, achievement | mark: made an enemy | tags: commit:career | chance: 65
- R | say yes, quit your job the same week, and throw yourself in | binds | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | tags: commit:career | chance: 60
- G | take it on and keep it just as it always was | v: tradition | identity | tags: commit:career | chance: 55
- W>B | set it up as a proper company, every contract in writing, and yourself in charge | v: power, security | tags: commit:career | chance: 60
- U>R | keep your day job and run the business secretly on the side until it flies | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: the day job forbids side work; backfire: dismissed when found out | tags: commit:career | chance: 40
- B>G | buy it cheap, and build it into a business the family will inherit | v: tradition, power | binds | tags: commit:career | chance: 75
- R>W | take it on with fire, and make it the heart of the neighbourhood | v: benevolence, stimulation | tags: commit:career | chance: 75
- G>U | work there for a season first, learning the trade from the inside | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | tags: commit:career | chance: 72
works: The first year is hard, but the books balance and the regulars stay.
works: By the second spring the business is unmistakably {Ns}.
fails: The money runs out faster than the plan said it would.
fails: The business survives, but it eats every evening and weekend {N} has.
